{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def next_smallest_palindrome(n):\n    # Convert to string and find the next palindrome\n    s = str(n + 1)\n    \n    while True:\n        # Check if current number is palindrome\n        if s == s[::-1]:\n            return int(s)\n        \n        # Make it a palindrome by mirroring left half to right half\n        length = len(s)\n        mid = length // 2\n        \n        if length % 2 == 0:\n            # Even length\n            left_half = s[:mid]\n            candidate = left_half + left_half[::-1]\n        else:\n            # Odd length\n            left_half = s[:mid]\n            middle = s[mid]\n            candidate = left_half + middle + left_half[::-1]\n        \n        if int(candidate) > n:\n            return int(candidate)\n        \n        # If mirroring doesn't give us a larger number, increment the middle part\n        if length % 2 == 0:\n            left_num = int(s[:mid]) + 1\n            left_str = str(left_num)\n            if len(left_str) > mid:\n                # Overflow, need one more digit\n                s = '1' + '0' * (length - 1) + '1'\n                return int(s)\n            left_str = left_str.zfill(mid)\n            s = left_str + left_str[::-1]\n        else:\n            left_part = s[:mid+1]\n            left_num = int(left_part) + 1\n            left_str = str(left_num)\n            if len(left_str) > mid + 1:\n                # Overflow, need one more digit\n                s = '1' + '0' * length + '1'\n                return int(s)\n            left_str = left_str.zfill(mid + 1)\n            s = left_str + left_str[-2::-1]"}
