{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all Ludic numbers up to n using the sieve method.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # Take the first number as the next Ludic number\n        next_ludic = numbers[0]\n        ludic.append(next_ludic)\n        \n        # If this is the first Ludic number (1), just remove it\n        if next_ludic == 1:\n            numbers = numbers[1:]\n        else:\n            # Remove every k-th element where k is the current Ludic number\n            new_numbers = []\n            for i, num in enumerate(numbers):\n                if (i + 1) % next_ludic != 0:\n                    new_numbers.append(num)\n            numbers = new_numbers\n    \n    return ludic"}
