{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all ludic numbers <= n using the ludic sieve algorithm.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # Take the first number as ludic\n        first = numbers.pop(0)\n        ludic.append(first)\n        \n        if not numbers:\n            break\n            \n        # Remove every k-th element where k is the ludic number we just found\n        k = first\n        if k == 1:\n            continue\n            \n        # Remove elements at positions k-1, 2k-1, 3k-1, etc. (0-indexed)\n        new_numbers = []\n        for i, num in enumerate(numbers):\n            if (i + 1) % k != 0:\n                new_numbers.append(num)\n        numbers = new_numbers\n    \n    return ludic"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the nth Bell number using dynamic programming with Bell triangle.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    bell = [[0 for i in range(n+1)] for j in range(n+1)]\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i+1):\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i-1][j-1] + bell[i][j-1]\n    \n    return bell[n][0]"}
